## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical TTL-state reasoning and side-input-driven re-enrichment under at-least-once guarantees.

## Key Concepts
- TTL cache per merchant
- Side-input rule versioning
- Exactly-once-like semantics via idempotent emits and commitOffsets
- Re-enrichment on rule updates

## Code Example
```javascript
function enrich(txn, ctx) {
  const rule = cache.get(txn.merchantId);
  if (!rule || rule.expiry < now()) {
    emit({ ...txn, riskScore: null, ruleVersion: rule?.ruleVersion ?? 0 });
  } else {
    emit({ ...txn, riskScore: rule.riskScore, ruleVersion: rule.ruleVersion });
  }
}
```

